{% comment %}
  What is next - one meeting, as large as the box allows.

  The countdown is worked out *here*, against the clock at the moment of
  drawing, rather than taken from the payload. The payload's countdown was true
  when Google was last asked, which is up to ten minutes ago, and "in 49 min"
  on a wall when the thing starts in four is worse than no clock at all. Every
  card carries the minutes since midnight it starts at, so the subtraction is
  cheap and always current - and the design declares `tick: 300`, so the server
  redraws it every five minutes whether or not anything was fetched.

  Which meeting is "next" is decided the same way and for the same reason: a
  meeting that has started since the last fetch is not the next one any more.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign day = calendar -%}
{%- assign hh = "now" | date: "%H" | times: 60 -%}
{%- assign now_mins = "now" | date: "%M" | plus: hh -%}

{%- assign running = false -%}
{%- assign coming = false -%}
{%- for event in day.upcoming -%}
  {%- if event.start_minutes > now_mins -%}
    {%- if coming == false %}{% assign coming = event %}{% endif -%}
  {%- elsif running == false and event.end_minutes > now_mins -%}
    {%- assign running = event -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- assign card = coming -%}
{%- if running %}{% assign card = running %}{% endif -%}

{%- comment %} Out of day, but not out of calendar.
  "Nothing left today" with nothing beside it is a panel reporting what it does
  not know, and it is what this design showed every evening from six o'clock
  until midnight. `next_any` is the next thing anywhere in the window that was
  actually fetched, so the card carries on being a card - tomorrow's first
  meeting rather than a shrug - and the fact that today is finished becomes the
  line above it instead of the whole picture. When the widget was only asked
  about today there is genuinely nothing to show, and only then does the empty
  branch below draw. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign later = false -%}
{%- if card == false and day.next_any and day.next_any.start_minutes > now_mins -%}
  {%- comment %} Only when it is genuinely still ahead. A payload is up to ten
    minutes old, and `next_any` was the next thing when Google was last asked -
    so it has to be checked against the clock at the moment of drawing, exactly
    as the countdown is. Left unchecked, a meeting that started while nobody
    was looking is drawn as the next one with "now" beside it. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- assign card = day.next_any -%}
  {%- comment %} "Nothing left today" only when it is genuinely not today. A
    horizon shorter than the day leaves a late meeting out of `upcoming` while
    it is still ahead of you, and announcing that today is over across the top
    of it would be the one kind of wrong a calendar is never forgiven for. That
    case wants the ordinary countdown, which is what falls out of leaving
    `later` alone. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- if day.next_any_day != "Today" %}{% assign later = true %}{% endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign box_w = shape.width | at_least: 110 -%}
{%- assign box_h = shape.height | at_least: 60 -%}
{%- comment %} Padding off the shorter side rather than off the width: a
  full-width band is 800 by 80, and a twentieth of the width either side of it
  is more than half the height gone before anything is drawn. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign shorter = box_w | at_most: box_h -%}
{%- assign pad = shorter | divided_by: 7 | at_least: 7 | at_most: 24 -%}

<div class="screen">
  {%- if card == false -%}
    {%- comment %} Nothing ahead anywhere in what was asked for. What is left
      to draw is the day that has just gone, and it is worth drawing: seven
      meetings and five hours of them is a *shape*, and a sentence saying so is
      the one thing on this panel nobody would cross a room to read. {% endcomment -%}
    {%- assign held = day.today.total | plus: day.all_day.size -%}
    {%- assign said = day.empty_label | default: "Nothing left today" -%}
    {%- capture summary -%}
      {% if day.today.total > 0 %}{{ day.today.total }} today, {{ day.today.busy_text }} of it{% if day.today.last_end != blank %}, done by {{ day.today.last_end }}{% endif %}{% elsif day.all_day.size > 0 %}{{ day.all_day.size }} all-day, nothing timed{% endif %}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- comment %} A shallow box is a different picture, not a smaller one. Full
      width and eighty pixels tall, the column below sizes its words off the
      height and produces ten-point type in the middle of 800 pixels of white.
      Laid along the band instead, the same words are thirty. {% endcomment -%}
    {%- if shape.rows <= 3 and box_w > 300 -%}
      <div class="content layout layout--row layout--center" style="gap: {{ pad }}px; padding: {{ pad }}px {{ pad | times: 1.5 | round }}px">
        <span class="i i-calendar-check i-md" style="flex: none"></span>
        <p class="t-bold truncate" style="font-size: {{ box_h | divided_by: 2.6 | round | at_least: 14 | at_most: 30 }}px">
          {{ said }}
        </p>
        {% if box_w > 460 and summary != blank %}
          <p class="t-xs truncate" style="flex: none">{{ summary }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
    <div class="content layout layout--col layout--center" style="gap: {{ pad | divided_by: 2 }}px; padding: {{ pad }}px">
      {% if box_w > 170 %}
        <span class="i i-calendar-check {% if shape.rows > 5 %}i-xl{% elsif shape.rows > 3 %}i-lg{% else %}i-md{% endif %}"></span>
      {% endif %}
      {%- comment %} Bounded by the width as well as the height. A two-column
        column is 133 pixels wide and 480 tall, and sized off the height alone
        "Nothing left today" is set at 34 and clipped mid-word. {% endcomment -%}
      {%- assign said_size = box_w | divided_by: 7 | at_most: 34 -%}
      <p class="t-bold t-center clamp-2" style="font-size: {{ box_h | divided_by: 8 | at_most: said_size | at_least: 13 }}px; width: 100%; line-height: 1.1">
        {{ said }}
      </p>

      {% if shape.rows > 3 and held > 0 %}
        {%- comment %} The day behind you, drawn rather than counted. Hatched
          because every one of these is over - the same fill the ribbon uses
          for what is done, so the two designs mean the same thing by it. {% endcomment -%}
        <div class="fit" style="flex: none; width: 100%; max-width: 320px">
          <div style="position: relative; border: 2px solid var(--ink); width: 100%;
                      height: {{ box_h | divided_by: 9 | at_least: 10 | at_most: 20 }}px">
            {%- assign open = day.window.open -%}
            {%- assign span = day.window.span | at_least: 120 -%}
            {% for event in day.events %}
              {%- assign from = event.start_minutes | minus: open -%}
              {%- assign until = event.end_minutes | minus: open -%}
              {%- if until > 0 and from < span -%}
                {%- if from < 0 %}{% assign from = 0 %}{% endif -%}
                {%- if until > span %}{% assign until = span %}{% endif -%}
                {%- assign at = from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
                {%- assign wide = until | minus: from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
                <span style="position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: {{ at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%;
                             width: {{ wide | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; min-width: 3px;
                             background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--ink) 0 2px, var(--paper) 2px 5px)"></span>
              {%- endif -%}
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
          <p class="t-xs t-center" style="margin-top: 4px">{{ summary }}</p>
        </div>
      {% elsif shape.rows > 3 %}
        <p class="t-sm t-center truncate" style="width: 100%">Nothing on it at all.</p>
      {% endif %}

      {% if shape.rows > 5 and day.all_day.size > 0 %}
        <p class="with-icon t-xs truncate" style="max-width: 100%">
          <span class="i i-calendar i-xs"></span>
          <span class="truncate">
            {% for entry in day.all_day %}{{ entry.title }}{% unless forloop.last %} &middot; {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
          </span>
        </p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment %} Minutes to go, or minutes left of the thing you are in.
      Both are the same subtraction against the same clock. {% endcomment -%}
    {%- assign until = card.start_minutes | minus: now_mins -%}
    {%- assign left = card.end_minutes | minus: now_mins -%}

    {%- assign chars = card.title | size | at_least: 8 -%}
    {%- assign lines = 2 -%}
    {%- if shape.rows < 4 %}{% assign lines = 1 %}{% endif -%}

    {%- comment %} Everything that is not the title, counted with the gap it
      brings with it. Leaving the gaps out is what wrapped "Lunch with Marco"
      onto a second line the box did not have room for - and a clamped line
      clipped in half reads as a broken screen rather than as a long title. {% endcomment -%}
    {%- assign gap = pad | divided_by: 2 -%}
    {%- assign spent = 0 -%}
    {%- if shape.rows > 2 %}{% assign spent = spent | plus: 26 | plus: gap %}{% endif -%}
    {%- if shape.rows > 4 %}{% assign spent = spent | plus: 30 | plus: gap %}{% endif -%}
    {%- if shape.rows <= 2 %}{% assign spent = spent | plus: 22 | plus: gap %}{% endif -%}
    {%- assign roomy = false -%}
    {%- if shape.rows > 6 and extension.values.show_location != false and card.location != blank -%}
      {%- assign roomy = true -%}
      {%- assign spent = spent | plus: 30 | plus: gap -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if notices.size > 0 %}{% assign spent = spent | plus: 34 %}{% endif -%}

    {%- assign room_h = box_h | minus: pad | minus: pad | minus: spent | at_least: 20 -%}
    {%- assign per_line = chars | divided_by: lines | plus: 2 -%}
    {%- assign by_width = box_w | minus: pad | minus: pad | times: 100 | divided_by: per_line | divided_by: 52 -%}
    {%- assign by_height = room_h | times: 92 | divided_by: 100 | divided_by: lines -%}
    {%- assign title_size = by_width | at_most: by_height | at_most: 64 | at_least: 13 -%}

    <div class="content layout layout--col" style="justify-content: center; gap: {{ pad | divided_by: 2 }}px; padding: {{ pad }}px">
      {% if shape.rows > 2 %}
        <div class="with-icon" style="gap: 6px">
          {% if running %}
            <span class="badge">Now</span>
            <span class="t-bold truncate" style="font-size: {{ title_size | divided_by: 2 | at_least: 12 | at_most: 22 }}px">
              {{ left | at_least: 1 }} min left
            </span>
          {% elsif later %}
            {%- comment %} Two facts, and the order matters: today being over is
              why this card is showing something that is not today. {% endcomment -%}
            <span class="i i-calendar-check i-sm"></span>
            <span class="t-bold truncate" style="font-size: {{ title_size | divided_by: 2 | at_least: 12 | at_most: 22 }}px">
              Nothing left today
            </span>
          {% else %}
            <span class="i i-clock i-sm"></span>
            <span class="t-bold truncate" style="font-size: {{ title_size | divided_by: 2 | at_least: 12 | at_most: 22 }}px">
              {{ until | in_words }}{% if card.start_minutes >= 1440 %} &middot; tomorrow{% endif %}
            </span>
          {% endif %}
          {% if card.conflict %}<span class="i i-alert i-xs" title="Double booked"></span>{% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      <p class="t-bold clamp-{{ lines }}" style="font-size: {{ title_size }}px; line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.02em">
        {{ card.title }}
      </p>

      {% if shape.rows > 4 %}
        <p class="t-mono t-bold truncate" style="font-size: {{ title_size | divided_by: 2 | at_least: 13 | at_most: 26 }}px">
          {% if later %}<span class="t-upper">{{ day.next_any_day }}</span> {% endif %}{{ card.start }}{% if card.end != blank %} &ndash; {{ card.end }}{% endif %}
        </p>
      {% elsif shape.rows <= 2 or later %}
        {%- comment %} A band has no room for the chip above, so the one line
          under the title has to carry both the time and the state - and a
          meeting you are sitting in reads "until", not "now".

          A card showing tomorrow needs the same line for a different reason:
          between three and four rows there is no room for the full time, and
          the chip above has been spent saying that today is over. A day and a
          time is the least that card can be worth looking at. {% endcomment -%}
        <p class="t-mono t-bold truncate" style="font-size: {{ title_size | divided_by: 2 | at_least: 11 | at_most: 18 }}px">
          {% if running %}
            {{ card.start }}&ndash;{{ card.end }} &middot; {{ left | at_least: 1 }} min left
          {% elsif later %}
            {{ day.next_any_day }} {{ card.start }} &middot; nothing left today
          {% else %}
            {{ card.start }} &middot; {{ until | in_words }}
          {% endif %}
        </p>
      {% endif %}

      {% if roomy %}
        <p class="with-icon truncate" style="font-size: {{ title_size | divided_by: 2.6 | round | at_least: 12 | at_most: 20 }}px">
          <span class="i i-{% if card.remote %}video{% else %}pin{% endif %} i-sm"></span>
          <span class="truncate">{{ card.location }}</span>
        </p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {% comment %}
    Where another extension gets to say something on this screen. Glyphs like
    dashboard warning lights, with the loudest one's words beside them when the
    box is wide enough to carry them.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if notices.size > 0 and shape.rows > 2 %}
    <div class="notice-strip" style="padding: 6px {{ pad }}px">
      {% for notice in notices %}
        {% if notice.overflow %}
          <span class="notice notice--more">+{{ notice.overflow }}</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="notice notice--{{ notice.level }}" title="{{ notice.text }}">
            <span class="i i-{{ notice.icon }}"></span>
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

      {% if shape.wide and notices[0].text != blank %}
        <span class="notice-said">{{ notices[0].text }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
